  "correction_rules": [
    "When sentiment is negative (≤ 0), reduce forecast by 5-10% to account for downward pressure.",
    "After a price spike (≥ 75), apply a 10-15 day cooling-off period with gradual mean reversion to avoid overshoot.",
    "If true outcome is consistently below forecast (persistent underperformance), adjust downward bias by 3-5% for next period.",
    "For sentiment history with multiple consecutive 0.00 values, assume low volatility and apply a 2-3% downward correction to avoid overconfidence.",
    "If forecast is > 70 and true outcome is < 65, apply a 10% downward correction to prevent overestimation in high volatility zones.",
    "When sentiment includes 0.20 or higher, increase forecast sensitivity to recent true values (use 3-day weighted average for adjustment)."
  ]
}
